// §14 entry 6 -- `:nativus` in a wire struct -> EXS-E0321.
//
// §5.2: "Byte order is in the type. `:nativus` is legal in-process and
// **illegal in any `@transitus` type** (EXS-E0321)." `@transitus` marks a
// type as a wire format, and a wire format has no "native" byte order to
// speak of -- only the two ends' agreement, which is exactly what `:maior`
// (explicit big-endian, attested throughout §5.2's own `Capitulum` and
// `DeModFrame` examples) commits to and `:nativus` refuses to.
//
// RUNS: the @transitus layout checker (wire-codec branch) now rejects this.
// compiler/x86_64/ast/ and cst/ are no longer empty (cst/parse.inc alone is
// 5048 lines); `exsc aedifica --hospes x86_64-linux --diagnostica json`, run
// directly against this file, exits 1 and emits exactly one diagnostic --
// {"code":"EXS-E0321",...,"message":":nativus in a @transitus type",...,
// "snippet":"signum:    u32:nativus"} -- confirmed, not assumed.

@transitus
publica structura Capitulum {
    signum:    u32:nativus
    versio:    u8
    genus:     u8
    reserva:   u16:maior
    longitudo: u32:maior
}

// TEST: entry=6 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0321 status=run
